Z||000010||Fiero5||10-02-2000||02:15 PM||||"Personally I dont like it, but heres a picture of a car with one. This pic is one of the better ones, It looks even more ridiculous in the other photos."<P>That wing is not a fair reproduction of an actual Lambo "Countach" wing. It has only one stantion support in the center. This pic below is an actual replica of a Countach wing. Of course the car isn't too shabby either!<BR>I may take a picture of a black Fiero GT at the same angle, and paste this wing on it to see what an actual Countach spoiler would look like on a Fiero. Maybe do a fastback and a notchback. Hmmmm.<P>------------------<BR>                                                  <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/nice8bg.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fiero5||10-02-2000||02:22 PM||||Heres a better angle so you can see the two  stantions and so forth. It is a huge wing, but remember, many Countach kits are made to go on a stock non stretched Fiero. The wing stays proportionate to the size of the car. Maybe with a slightly lowered Fiero it would look alot better? I know most Fiero based Countach kits do lower the car also. Just a thought.<P>------------------<BR>                                                   <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/nice9bg.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fiero5||10-02-2000||02:36 PM||||How about having the doors on your Fiero open like Lamborghini doors do? Lambo doors would be sooo cool!<P>------------------<BR>                                                    <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/car6.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Songman||10-02-2000||06:08 PM||||I am more bothered by the GTO on the window of that car in the picture than I am by the wing on the back. I love my Fieros but GTOs were my first Pontiac love... ||||reg||1
Z||000014||rockcrawl||10-02-2000||06:37 PM||||OK, here's some more info about Joe Pistono's 1984 Fiero 'GTO' pictured above. The Ground effects and side scoops are from Mecham Racing in Arizona. The wing is a Formula wing from Pegasus Engineering. All that stuff was done before 1987. Cars and Concepts T tops were added in '88. The wing does have two stanchions, but they are closer together than the countach wing. <P>Fiero5, are you sure thats a replica Countach? It looks damn good, except that it has 25th anniversary wheels and it's not an anniversary model. Do you know who makes that kit, it looks very accurate.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fiero5||10-03-2000||01:48 PM||||I was talking to Jody Lemos on Sunday at the Stratham NH car show, which he placed first in the Fiero class by the way, and he was mentioning this thread and said the wing in that pic earlier looked like it was from a Piranha kit. Sure enough, here is a pic of a Piranha kit. Looks the same to me.<P>------------------<BR>                                                                       <IMG SRC="http://www.cadgraph.com.pl/fiero/images/Kits/WEB_Stil_Piranha_CJK_str366.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fiero5||10-03-2000||02:03 PM||||Ok, many of you have questioned the Black Countach that I posted here, saying it looked too good for a kit. Here is the link to the site I snagged the pics off of: <A HREF="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/specs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/specs.html</A> <BR>Here is a shot of the engine in that awsome Countach kit<P>------------------<BR>                                                                        <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/engine1bg.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fiero5||10-03-2000||02:14 PM||||"The wing does have two stanchions, but they are closer together than the countach wing."<P>They must be really close together, as I don't even see a shadow from the back side stantion. Either way, I would't call that a fair copy of Countach spoiler by any means. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||rockcrawl||10-03-2000||07:55 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lambowing2.jpg"> <BR>This picture shows the two stanchions a little better. When I got my Countach kit, the wing was un-assembled (as requested). The stanchions could be placed anywhere across the length of the wing, and the end plates could be left off if desired. So if someone wanted a Lambo wing on a Fiero, it would be fairly easy to do.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
